webpackJsonp([0x81b8806e4260],{430:function(e,t){e.exports={data:{site:{siteMetadata:{title:"Mihail Eric",subtitle:"Engineer, researcher, educator.",copyright:"Copyright",menu:[{label:"Blog",path:"/blog/"},{label:"Projects",path:"/projects/"},{label:"Teaching",path:"/teaching/"}],author:{name:"Mihail Eric",email:"mihail911@gmail.com",twitter:"mihail_eric",github:"mihail911",linkedin:"mihaileric"}}},markdownRemark:{id:"/Users/mihaileric/Documents/Projects/mihail911.github.io/src/pages/pages/2015-05-01---about/index.md absPath of file >>> MarkdownRemark",html:'<p>I optimize for impact. I strive to work with smart people to do amazing things. If you are a misfit, a rebel, or a troublemaker working on something interesting, feel free to <a href="mailto:mihail911@gmail.com">drop me a line.</a></p>\n<p>I’m a researcher, engineer, and educator currently working on the future of conversational artificial intelligence at <a href="https://developer.amazon.com/alexa-skills-kit/conversational-ai">Alexa AI</a>. I’m also building <a href="https://www.confetti.ai/">Confetti AI</a>. A few things I’m proud of:</p>\n<h3>Research</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>I’ve been published at the top artificial intelligence conferences in the world. My work has also gotten <a href="https://venturebeat.com/2019/12/04/amazon-proposes-a-home-robot-that-asks-you-questions-when-its-confused/">news coverage</a>. Check out <a href="/projects">my past projects</a> for a full list of publications.</li>\n<li>I spent several years in the <a href="https://nlp.stanford.edu/">Stanford Natural Language Processing Group</a>, where I had the great fortune to work with <a href="https://nlp.stanford.edu/manning/">Christopher Manning</a>, <a href="https://cs.stanford.edu/~pliang/">Percy Liang</a>, and <a href="https://web.stanford.edu/~cgpotts/">Christopher Potts</a>.</li>\n<li>I think and write about trends in AI research. People have found my <a href="/posts/nlp-trends-acl-2019/">past</a> <a href="/posts/ml-trends-neurips-2019/">writeups</a> <a href="/posts/review-of-sigdial-semdial-2017/">helpful</a>. </li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Engineering</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>I was the 8th engineer at <a href="https://rideos.ai/">RideOS</a> a Sequoia VC-backed autonomous mobility startup.</li>\n<li>I’m problem-driven (not tool-driven) so I build across the full engineering stack from <a href="https://www.mihaileric.com/posts/building-a-deep-learning-computer/">hardware</a> to <a href="https://www.mihaileric.com/posts/state-of-the-art-question-answering-streamlit-huggingface/">software</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Education</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>I have studied at the <a href="https://www.exeter.edu/">top institutions</a> in <a href="https://www.stanford.edu/">the world</a>.</li>\n<li>I believe in paying things forward, so I <a href="https://www.confetti.ai">build tools</a> and <a href="/posts/complete-artificial-intelligence-undergraduate-course-plan/">create resources</a> to help people learn. Check out my <a href="/blog/">blog</a> to see what I teach about.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>What Keeps Me Up These Nights</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>How do we prepare the next generation of artificial intelligence practitioners to be successful in their careers? <a href="https://www.confetti.ai/">Confetti AI</a> is my ongoing answer.</li>\n<li>Humans produce <a href="https://techjury.net/blog/how-much-data-is-created-every-day/#gref">2.5 quintillion bytes of data every day</a>. In that sea of noise, how do we find the stuff that really matters?</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>News</h2>\n<p><strong>October 2020</strong>: I created a primer on machine learning theory important for ML interviews. <a href="https://www.confetti.ai/assets/ml-primer/ml_primer.pdf">Check it out!</a><br>\n<strong>September 2020</strong>: I wrote up a post describing how to build a deployable, state-of-the-art question-answering system over all of Wikipedia with just 60 lines of Python: <a href="/posts/state-of-the-art-question-answering-streamlit-huggingface/">post</a> and <a href="https://github.com/mihail911/question-answering-with-streamlit">code</a>.<br>\n<strong>July 2020</strong>: Our paper on task-oriented conversation modeling with unstructured knowledge access was presented at <a href="https://www.sigdial.org/files/workshops/conference21/pdf/2020.sigdial-1.35.pdf">SIGDial 2020</a>.<br>\n<strong>December 2019</strong>: After an eventful week at <a href="https://nips.cc/">NeurIPS 2019</a>, I wrote a post describing some of the <a href="/posts/ml-trends-neurips-2019/">key trends in machine learning today</a>.<br>\n<strong>November 2019</strong>: <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1912.00915.pdf">Our paper</a> on resolving ambiguity in vision and language navigation will be presented at <a href="https://aaai.org/Conferences/AAAI-20/">AAAI 2020</a> and <a href="https://nips.cc/">NeurIPS 2019</a> and was also featured in <a href="https://venturebeat.com/2019/12/04/amazon-proposes-a-home-robot-that-asks-you-questions-when-its-confused/">VentureBeat</a>!<br>\n<strong>October 2019</strong>: I’m co-organizing the <a href="https://sites.google.com/view/2ndnlp4convai/">2nd NLP for Conversational AI Workshop</a> at ACL 2020! If you love NLP and dialogue systems, we look forward to seeing you in Seattle.<br>\n<strong>August 2019</strong>: I wrote a blog post describing <a href="/posts/nlp-trends-acl-2019/">trends in modern NLP</a>, based on my trip to <a href="http://www.acl2019.org/EN/index.xhtml">ACL 2019</a>.<br>\n<strong>July 2019</strong>: We just released a modified version of the <a href="https://www.repository.cam.ac.uk/handle/1810/294507">MultiWOZ dataset</a> with corrected dialogue state annotations. For a description of the dataset, check out <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1907.01669">our writeup</a>.<br>\n<strong>June 2019</strong>: I’ve been collecting a <a href="https://github.com/mihail911/nlp-library">list of essential papers in NLP</a> for practitioners and researchers. Feel free to submit a pull request, if there’s a paper you think should be there!<br>\n<strong>February 2018</strong>: I led a Deep Learning Workshop at the Harvard Westlake School’s annual hackathon. Check out the <a href="/Deep-HWack-f969afea417b85c4662cd613529f0465.pdf">slides here</a> and the <a href="https://github.com/mihail911/deep-hwack">accompanying code</a>.    </p>',frontmatter:{title:"About me",date:null,description:null}}},pathContext:{}}}});
